<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edward Cornwallis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1713">1713</a>–<a href="/years/1776">1776</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edward Cornwallis was a British army officer and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> from 1749 to 1752. In 1749 he founded Halifax as a naval base and new capital with about 2,500 settlers. During conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikmaq">Mi'kmaq</a> in Father Le Loutre's War he offered bounties for Mi'kmaq scalps, which has made him a controversial figure. He later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-cornwallis.jpg" alt="Edward Cornwallis" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joshua Reynolds · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EdwardCornwallisArtGalleryofNovaScotia1756.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
